<p><strong>Reactant (Left):</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Zirconocene cation (Zr with two Cp rings)</li>
<li>An ethylene (H2C=3DCH2) coordinated to Zr in a side-on manner (=CE=B7=
=C2=B2-ethylene)</li>
<li>A methyl group (CH3) directly bonded to Zr</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Transition State (Middle):</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Zirconocene cation</li>
<li>The ethylene is inserting into the Zr-CH3 bond</li>
<li>Four-membered ring forming between Zr-C(ethylene)-C(ethylene)-C(methyl)=
</li>
<li>Dashed lines indicate partial bonds</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Product (Right):</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Zirconocene cation</li>
<li>Propyl group (CH2-CH2-CH3) bonded to Zr</li>
<li>The ethylene has inserted into the Zr-CH3 bond forming a new Zr-C bond =
to the propyl chain</li>
</ul>
<p>This is the Cossee-Arlman mechanism for olefin polymerization with a zir=
conocene catalyst.</p>
<p>Now I need to build these three structures:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Reactant</strong>: Cp2Zr(CH3)(=CE=B7=C2=B2-C2H4)+ - a zirconoce=
ne with methyl and side-on ethylene</li>
<li><strong>Transition State</strong>: The 4-membered ring intermediate wit=
h partial bonds</li>
<li><strong>Product</strong>: Cp2Zr(propyl)+ - zirconocene with n-propyl gr=
oup</li>
</ol>
<p>Let me start by checking available fragments and templates. I'll need:</=
p>
<ul>
<li>Cp rings (cyclopentadienyl)</li>
<li>Zirconium metal center</li>
<li>Methyl group</li>
